  },
  {
    exam: 'NISM Series XV: Research Analyst',
    fee: 'Rs 1,500 plus payment-gateway charges',
    format: '2 hours, 100 marks (80 questions plus 5 case sets), pass mark 60%, 25% negative marking',
    fit: 'Equity research and investment analysis. NISM writes this exam for people working as research analysts and does not mention students, so confirm that registration is open to you before you pay.',
  },
  {
    exam: 'SEBI Investor Awareness Test',
    fee: 'Free',
    format: '60 minutes, 50 questions, pass mark 50%, valid 2 years',
    fit: 'A no-cost first try to see if markets interest you at all.',
  },
];

const compareRows = [
  {
    cert: 'NISM Series exams',
    issuer: 'NISM',
    cost: 'Rs 1,500 plus gateway charges for the common ones; some cost Rs 3,000',
    proves: 'You passed a market-regulation exam anyone can verify. Valid for 3 years from the exam date, then renew before it lapses.',
    rung: 'Rung 1',
  },
  {
    cert: 'GST Practitioner enrolment exam',
    issuer: 'NACIN, for enrolment under the GST system',
    cost: 'Fee set by NACIN. Secondary sources report Rs 500 per attempt at the 2018-19 sittings. Training fees vary widely',
    proves: 'Enrolment on the GST portal, then an NACIN exam within the notified time. The last NACIN sitting on record was 12 December 2019, so check the portal before paying any trainer.',
    rung: 'Rung 1, but not bookable today',
  },
  {
    cert: 'Tally Bookkeeper Professional Certificate',
    issuer: 'Tally Education, on Coursera',
    cost: 'Listed as free to enrol, with a Coursera subscription option; centre courses cost more',
    proves: 'TallyPrime, payables and receivables, GST entries: about 125 hours across 3 courses. Tally Education says its certificates last for life and can be verified on its site.',
    rung: 'Rung 2',
  },
  {
    cert: 'Power BI Data Analyst Associate (PL-300)',
    issuer: 'Microsoft',
    cost: 'Priced by country. Microsoft\'s page shows no rupee figure; one guide lists USD 165 and Indian guides quote roughly Rs 4,000 to Rs 8,000. Confirm on the booking page',
    proves: 'Power Query, data modelling, DAX, dashboards. Renews every 12 months, free, through an online assessment.',
    rung: 'Rung 2',
  },
  {
    cert: 'Google Data Analytics Professional Certificate',
    issuer: 'Google, on Coursera',
    cost: 'Coursera charges USD 49 a month after a free trial; it lists 6 months at 10 hours a week',
    proves: 'Spreadsheets, SQL, Tableau and a capstone. The 75% job-outcome figure comes from a 2022 Coursera survey of US graduates.',
    rung: 'Rung 2',
  },
  {
    cert: 'NPTEL / SWAYAM courses',
    issuer: 'IIT-run NPTEL on the SWAYAM portal',
    cost: 'Learning is free; the optional proctored certification exam is Rs 1,000 per course',
    proves: 'Proctored exam result. Counts for credit only if your college approves the course.',
    rung: 'Rung 3',
  },
  {
    cert: 'Local institute certificate (Tally + GST, Advanced Excel, SAP FICO, Power BI)',
    issuer: 'The institute that sold the course',
    cost: 'Power BI courses are listed from Rs 4,800 to Rs 77,000 across 14 providers, about 16 times apart',
    proves: 'Attendance. Any proof of skill has to come from what you build.',
    rung: 'Rung 4',
  },
];

const feeTrapRows = [
  { subject: 'Power BI', range: 'Rs 4,800 to Rs 77,000 across 14 providers', spread: 'About 16 times apart; the middle provider is about Rs 20,400', source: 'Henry Harvin provider comparison, March 2025' },
  { subject: 'Tally with GST', range: 'Rs 5,000 to Rs 10,000 in one guide; Rs 6,000 to Rs 20,000 in another', spread: 'About 3 times apart in the wider range', source: 'BCIT World, 2023; SelectYourUniversity, August 2025' },
  { subject: 'SAP FICO basics', range: 'Rs 20,000 to Rs 40,000', spread: 'About 2 times apart', source: 'Entri, 2026' },
];

const laneCostRows = [
  { lane: 'Markets', route: 'SEBI Investor Awareness Test, one NISM exam (Series V-A or VIII), one NPTEL exam', cost: 'Rs 0 + Rs 1,500 + Rs 1,000 = Rs 2,500, plus gateway charges', share: 'About 25%' },
  { lane: 'Analysis', route: 'Microsoft Learn (free), PL-300 exam at the third-party estimate, one NPTEL exam', cost: 'Rs 4,000 to Rs 8,000 + Rs 1,000 = Rs 5,000 to Rs 9,000', share: 'About 50% to 90%' },
  { lane: 'Accounts and tax', route: 'Tally Authorised Learning Centre course at the listed range, one NPTEL exam', cost: 'Rs 6,000 to Rs 20,000 + Rs 1,000 = Rs 7,000 to Rs 21,000', share: 'About 70% to 210%' },
  { lane: 'For comparison: a middle-priced institute Power BI course', route: 'Course fee only, no exam fee', cost: 'About Rs 20,400', share: 'About 204%' },
];

const goalCards = [
  {
    tag: 'Business analyst, MIS, reporting',
    title: 'Excel, then Power BI',
    body: 'Free Microsoft Learn material first. Take PL-300 only after you have built two dashboards. The sibling guide on computer and data courses covers the full Excel, SQL, and Python sequence.',
    best: 'Best for: students who enjoy numbers more than filing.',
    watch: 'Watch out: PL-300 needs yearly renewal, and a badge without a dashboard behind it convinces nobody.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Markets, broking, wealth',
    title: 'NISM exams',
    body: 'Start with the free SEBI Investor Awareness Test, then a Rs 1,500 NISM exam that matches the role. NISM Series V-A is the mutual fund distributor exam, one of the few routes where a BCom student can later build an own client book. Distributors usually need a separate industry registration too, so check the current rules.',
    best: 'Best for: BCom students who like markets and can handle sales targets.',
    watch: 'Watch out: NISM certificates last 3 years from the exam date, and a lapsed one cannot be renewed.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Accounts, tax, audit support',
    title: 'TallyPrime plus GST knowledge',
    body: 'Do a TallyPrime course from a Tally Authorised Learning Centre, or the Tally Bookkeeper course on Coursera. Your BCom is one of the degrees Rule 83 lists for GST practitioner enrolment, but the NACIN exam that enrolment depends on has not been held since December 2019. Build GST knowledge now and treat the practitioner certificate as a possibility, not a plan.',
    best: 'Best for: a fast route to accounts executive or article-assistant work.',
    watch: 'Watch out: many local courses teach button-clicking. Ask to see a full-year entry set you can practise on.',
  },
  {
    tag: 'Still unsure',
    title: 'One free, credit-friendly course',
    body: 'Pick one SWAYAM or NPTEL course your college accepts. It costs nothing to learn, tests your interest, and may count for credit.',
    best: 'Best for: first-year students who do not want to spend before they know.',
    watch: 'Watch out: credit counts only if your university approves that exact course before you start.',
  },
];

const semesterPlan = [
  {
    num: 'Year 1',
    title: 'Learn free, spend nothing',
    body: 'Ask your department which SWAYAM courses it accepts for credit. Finish one. Take the free SEBI Investor Awareness Test. Learn spreadsheet basics from free sources. The aim is to find which of the three areas (accounts, markets, analysis) you can sit with for hours without boredom.',
  },
  {
    num: 'Year 2',
    title: 'Pick one lane and pay for one certificate',
    body: 'Choose the lane from Year 1. Accounts and tax: a TallyPrime course from a Tally Authorised Learning Centre, or the Tally Bookkeeper certificate on Coursera. Markets: study for one NISM exam and book it late in Year 2 or in Year 3, so its 3-year validity covers your job search. Analysis: a Power BI or Excel course with a project. Keep the total near the budget guide in the cost table above.',
  },
  {
    num: 'Year 3',
    title: 'Turn the certificate into proof',
    body: 'Build one piece of work you can show: a year of entries in TallyPrime for a small family shop, a one-page market note, or a sales dashboard from a public dataset. Then apply for internships with the work attached, not only the certificate. If you also want CA, CMA, or CS, this is the year to plan that separately.',
  },
];

const mistakeItems = [
  {
    num: '01',
    title: 'Buying a "job guarantee" certificate',
    body: 'No institute can guarantee a job at a fixed salary, and the salary figures on course pages usually come with no employer data behind them. Ask for placement lists you can call and check.',
  },
  {
    num: '02',
    title: 'Paying for a certificate you cannot verify with the issuer',
    body: 'Tally certificates come through Tally Authorised Learning Centres and can be checked on Tally Education\'s site. NISM and Microsoft issue their own. Before you pay a centre, confirm it is an authorised one and ask for the verification link. Paying several times the going rate for a paper with a different name is the most common waste.',
  },
  {
    num: '03',
    title: 'Stacking four certificates in one semester',
    body: 'Half-finished courses show on a resume as restlessness. One finished course with one project beats a list of five.',
  },
  {
    num: '04',
    title: 'Taking a NISM exam just to have it',
    body: 'A NISM certificate helps when you are applying to broking, wealth, or banking-sales roles. For an accounts job it adds very little. Match the exam to the job you are applying for.',
  },
  {
    num: '05',
    title: 'Assuming a free online course counts for credit',
    body: 'Credit transfer depends on your own university approving the course. Ask before you enrol, not after you finish.',
  },
  {
    num: '06',
    title: 'Booking a NISM exam in the first semester',
    body: 'The certificate is valid for 3 years from the exam date, and NISM says a lapsed certificate cannot be renewed. Passed in the first semester of a three-year BCom, it lapses around graduation, just when you start applying.',
  },
];

const faqItems = [
  {
    q: 'Which certificate courses are best for BCom students?',
    a: 'Choose by the job you want. For accounts and tax work, a TallyPrime course plus GST knowledge. For markets and wealth roles, a NISM exam such as Series V-A or VIII at Rs 1,500 each. For analyst and reporting roles, Excel then Power BI, with the PL-300 exam only after you have built two dashboards. Exam-body and software-maker certificates carry more weight than an institute\'s own paper.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I do a certificate course during BCom, or should I wait until after?',
    a: 'During is better for the cheap ones. Free SWAYAM and NPTEL courses, the free SEBI Investor Awareness Test, and one Rs 1,500 NISM exam fit easily around classes. Save bigger spending until you know your lane. Doing it before graduation also means your resume carries proof when internships open.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are short-term courses for commerce students worth the money?',
    a: 'They are worth it when the course ends in something you can show and the certificate can be verified. They are not worth it when the fee is several times what another provider charges for the same subject, or when the only promise is placement. Advertised fees for Tally with GST, for example, range from a few thousand rupees to Rs 20,000 depending on the institute.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What are the best professional courses for commerce students, and are certificates part of that list?',
    a: 'Professional courses usually means CA, CMA, CS, ACCA, CFA, and similar. Those are long qualifications with their own exams. Certificates are smaller and quicker, and they add a working skill on top of your BCom. They do not replace a professional qualification if your target role legally needs one, such as statutory audit.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can a BCom graduate become a GST practitioner?',
    a: 'Rule 83 of the CGST Rules lists a graduate or postgraduate degree in Commerce, Law, Banking, Business Administration or Business Management as one accepted qualification, along with Indian citizenship and other basic conditions. Enrolment is on the GST portal and depends on passing an NACIN exam within the notified time, which the rules set at two years for most enrolments. The catch is that the last NACIN sitting on record was 12 December 2019, and a December 2025 report says none has been held since. Check the GST portal and the NACIN site for the current position before paying any trainer.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need a finance background to take a NISM exam?',
    a: 'No. NISM\'s own FAQs for the Mutual Fund Distributors and Equity Derivatives exams say students and other interested people can sit them, not only people already working in the industry. The common papers cost Rs 1,500 plus payment-gateway charges, and NISM gives free soft-copy study workbooks after enrolment. The certificate is valid for 3 years from the exam date.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will my college give credit for an online certificate course?',
    a: 'Sometimes. UGC\'s 2021 credit framework lets a university allow up to 40% of the courses in a semester to be taken through SWAYAM, up from 20% earlier, but your own university must approve the course and decide how credits transfer. Ask your department for its approved SWAYAM list before you enrol.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is the SEBI Investor Awareness Test really free, and does it count for anything?',
    a: 'It is free on NISM\'s site: 50 questions in 60 minutes, pass mark 50%, and the certificate is valid for 2 years. It shows basic market literacy, not a job qualification, so use it to test your interest before you pay for a NISM exam.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do certificates expire, and when should I take them?',
    a: 'Some do. NISM certificates last 3 years from the exam date and a lapsed one cannot be renewed, so take the exam close to your job search. PL-300 renews every 12 months through a free online assessment. Tally Education says its certificates have lifetime validity.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I know if a certificate course is genuine?',
    a: 'Find out who actually issues the certificate. If it is Tally Education, Microsoft, NISM, or an IIT-run NPTEL exam, the issuer has a verification route. If the institute issues its own paper, ask whether an employer can confirm it online, ask for refund terms in writing, and ask to speak to two past students.',
  },
];
---

<BlogPostLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  category="college-degrees"
  publishedAt={publishedDateISO}
  publishedLabel={publishedDateLabel}
  authorName={authorName}
  authorUrl={authorUrl}
  authorRole={authorRole}
  ogImage={socialImageUrl}
  ogImageWidth={1200}
  ogImageHeight={630}
  jsonLdExtras={[
    {
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'FAQPage',
      mainEntity: faqItems.map((item) => ({
        '@type': 'Question',
        name: item.q,
        acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: item.a },
      })),
    },
  ]}
>
  <figure class="article-cover-visual">
    <img src={heroImageUrl} width="1600" height="900" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" alt="Indian BCom student comparing a verifiable certificate with spreadsheet practice at a sunlit classroom desk" title="Certificate Courses for BCom Students: Which Ones Employers Can Verify" />
    <figcaption>A useful certificate is one an employer can verify and connect to work you can actually show.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p class="lead-para">
    <strong>The best certificate courses for BCom students are the ones a stranger can verify: a NISM exam for markets and wealth roles, a TallyPrime certificate for accounts, and Power BI for reporting roles. The GST practitioner route is one to watch, not one you can book today.</strong>
    A certificate an employer cannot check is only a receipt. Pick the few that carry weight, prove them
    with one piece of real work, and your BCom starts building a high-income skill portfolio, which is
    what opens better income opportunities and moves you toward earlier financial freedom.
  </p>

  <div class="key-takeaways">
    <p class="key-takeaways__label">The short version</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Rank certificates by who issues them, not by how long the syllabus is. Exam bodies and software makers beat private institutes.</li>
      <li>Cheap and real: NISM exams at Rs 1,500, a free SEBI Investor Awareness Test, and free SWAYAM courses that may count for college credit.</li>
      <li>Compare fees and time the exam: Power BI courses are listed from Rs 4,800 to Rs 77,000, and a NISM certificate lasts 3 years, so a first-semester exam lapses around graduation.</li>
      <li>Next step: choose one lane (accounts, markets, or analysis), take one certificate, and build one project with it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/college-degrees/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students-at-a-glance-summary.webp" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Four-rung summary of certificate courses for BCom students: exam bodies, software vendors, college credit, and institute certificates" title="At a glance: certificate courses for BCom students" />
    <figcaption>Rank certificates by who issues them, what they prove, and whether the skill can become visible work.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    Certificates make the most sense <em>during</em> your BCom, when fees are small and your weekly schedule has room. If you have already
    finished the degree and want CA, CMA, MBA, or other bigger routes, read
    <a href="/blog/college-degrees/best-courses-after-bcom-for-high-salary/">best courses after BCom for high salary</a>.
    For every path after graduation, see
    <a href="/blog/career-options/career-after-bcom-in-india/">career after BCom in India</a>. Browse more
    <a href="/blog/college-degrees/">college-degree guides</a> here too.
  </p>

  <nav class="jump-nav" aria-label="Article sections">
    <p class="jump-nav__label">Jump to section</p>
    <ul class="jump-nav__list">
      {jumpLinks.map((item) => (
        <li><a href={`#${item.id}`}>{item.label}</a></li>
      ))}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <h2 id="short-answer">The short answer</h2>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/college-degrees/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students-framework-short-answer.webp" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Framework panel contrasting common certificate-course advice with a verification-first decision rule for BCom students" title="The short answer: choose verifiable certificate proof" />
    <figcaption>Do not collect certificates by volume; choose evidence an employer can verify and understand.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    If you are looking for certificate courses for BCom students, do not start with a list of "top 10".
    Start with a question: <strong>who will vouch for this certificate if a recruiter phones them?</strong>
    NISM will vouch for its own exam. Tally Education will vouch for its own course. Your local institute
    will vouch only for itself.
  </p>

  <p>
    Students ask the same things again and again: which course goes with BCom, is Tally with GST enough,
    is SAP worth it, what can I do beside my degree. The honest answer is that the subject matters less
    than the issuer and the proof you build. Advertised fees for the same subject vary so much that a student can
    easily pay several times more for a paper that a Rs 1,500 exam or a maker's own certificate would have beaten.
  </p>

  <p>
    The Ministry of Education's
    <a href="https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleasePage.aspx?PRID=1999713" target="_blank" rel="noopener">AISHE 2021-22 survey</a>
    counts about 4.33 crore students in higher education, 78.9% of them undergraduates, and puts
    commerce at 13.3% of undergraduates. That is roughly 45 lakh commerce undergraduates at one time.
    A certificate a recruiter can check in one click sets you apart from that pool; one they cannot check does not.
  </p>

  <div class="callout callout--amber">
    <p class="callout__eyebrow">Common advice that misleads</p>
    <ul class="callout__list">
      <li>"Do any computer course, it looks good on the resume."</li>
      <li>"Tally with GST alone gets a job."</li>
      <li>"The more certificates, the better."</li>
      <li>"Placement guaranteed, so the fee is worth it."</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="callout__footer">
      An employer cannot check button-clicking from a paper. A certificate helps when it is verifiable
      and when you can show one thing you made with it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="ladder">The 4-Rung Certificate Ladder</h2>

  <p>
    <strong>The 4-Rung Certificate Ladder</strong> is a simple way to judge any certificate before you pay.
    Higher rung means more weight with an employer and usually a lower fee. Use it every time.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-grid">
    {ladderRungs.map((item) => (
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-card__label">{item.tag}</div>
        <div class="feature-card__title">{item.title}</div>
        <p class="feature-card__provider">{item.provider}</p>
        <p>{item.body}</p>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      A degree still matters: many jobs and professional routes need it, and the BCom itself is what makes
      you eligible for things like GST practitioner enrolment. The trap is degree-only thinking. A BCom
      with one verified certificate and one finished project beats a BCom with six course papers.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="rung-1">Rung 1: exam-body certificates (NISM and GST practitioner)</h2>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/college-degrees/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students-comparison-rung-exam-body-certificates.webp" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Comparison of NISM exam-body certificates by fee, format, validity, and the BCom job lane they support" title="Rung 1: exam-body certificates (NISM and GST practitioner)" />
    <figcaption>NISM’s exam-body route is useful because the issuer, format, and validity can be checked directly.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    <a href="https://www.nism.ac.in/certifications/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NISM</a>, the National Institute of Securities Markets, runs certification exams for the securities
    industry. The exams are online and remote-proctored, and the certificates stay valid for 3
    years from the exam date. NISM's own FAQs for the Mutual Fund Distributors and Equity Derivatives exams say
    students and other interested people can sit them, not only people already working in the industry.
    NISM gives free soft-copy study workbooks after enrolment.
  </p>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Exam</th>
          <th>Fee</th>
          <th>Format</th>
          <th>Useful for</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {nismRows.map((item) => (
          <tr>
            <td data-label="Exam"><strong>{item.exam}</strong></td>
            <td data-label="Fee">{item.fee}</td>
            <td data-label="Format">{item.format}</td>
            <td data-label="Useful for">{item.fit}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">
    Fees, formats and pass marks are from NISM's own exam pages, checked in September 2026. A new attempt needs
    a fresh registration and fee, so practise on mock tests before booking. Confirm the current fee on NISM before you pay.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--teal">
    <p>
      <strong>Why this rung matters for your income.</strong> A Rs 1,500 exam that opens wealth, broking,
      and research doors is one of the cheapest steps in a BCom student's high-income skill portfolio.
      It works best when you can also explain markets in two clear minutes. Series V-A also opens mutual fund distribution,
      where income can grow with a client book you own instead of a salary band. Distributors usually need a separate
      registration, so check the current rules first.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    The GST practitioner route is different. Rule 83 of the CGST Rules lists a graduate or postgraduate
    degree in Commerce, Law, Banking, Business Administration, or Business Management as one accepted
    qualification, plus basic conditions such as Indian citizenship. You apply on the GST portal, and
    enrolment depends on passing an NACIN exam within the notified time. Secondary sources describe it as a
    computer-based test of 100 multiple-choice questions, 200 marks, with 100 needed to pass and no negative marking.
  </p>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      <strong>Check this before you pay any GST trainer.</strong> The last NACIN sitting on record was on
      12 December 2019, and a December 2025 report says no sitting has been held since. Sources also differ on
      exactly who must sit the exam. Confirm the current status on the GST portal and the NACIN site.
      Learning GST is still useful for accounts work. A trainer who promises a practitioner certificate by a fixed date has no way to promise that.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take: the scalable path</p>
    <p>
      If the exam reopens, GST practitioner enrolment is one of the few certificate routes that can grow into
      your own small practice: you can serve several small businesses at once and add services such as return
      filing and reconciliation. It scales through repeat clients and referrals, not through the certificate.
      Expect a slow start while you win your first few clients, and expect to keep learning as rules change.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="rung-2">Rung 2: software and vendor certificates</h2>

  <p>
    These matter when the employer uses the tool. A small accounting firm cares about TallyPrime. A
    finance-reporting team cares about Excel and Power BI.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Tally Bookkeeper Professional Certificate.</strong> Offered by Tally Education itself on
      Coursera. The listing shows about 4 months at 10 hours a week, around 125 hours across 3 courses:
      accounting basics, payables and receivables, and taxation with GST. Tally Education also certifies through
      Tally Authorised Learning Centres and says its certificates can be verified on its
      <a href="https://tallyeducation.com/tepl/certificate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">verification page</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Power BI Data Analyst Associate (PL-300).</strong> Microsoft's exam covers Power Query,
      data modelling, DAX, and visuals (see <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/credentials/certifications/data-analyst-associate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Microsoft Learn</a>). Microsoft offers a free study guide and practice assessment, and
      you can renew the certificate free every 12 months through an online assessment. The exam is priced by country
      and the Microsoft page shows no rupee figure, so check the booking page.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Data Analytics Professional Certificate.</strong> Coursera lists 9 courses, 6 months
      at 10 hours a week, covering spreadsheets, SQL, Tableau, and a capstone. Coursera says 75% of
      graduates report a positive career outcome within six months. That figure is a 2022 Coursera survey of
      US graduates, not an independent study of Indian BCom graduates.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    For the full Excel, SQL, and Python sequence and how to judge each course, read
    <a href="/blog/college-degrees/best-computer-and-data-science-courses-for-commerce-students/">best computer and data science courses for commerce students</a>.
    For the wider skill stack beyond certificates, see
    <a href="/blog/skills/best-skills-for-commerce-students-to-learn/">best skills for commerce students to learn</a>.
    Here the question is narrower: which certificate papers are worth holding at all.
  </p>

  <h2 id="rung-3">Rung 3: SWAYAM and NPTEL, and college credit</h2>

  <p>
    NPTEL courses on the SWAYAM portal are free to learn. The optional proctored certification exam is
    Rs 1,000 per course, as <a href="https://swayam.gov.in/nc_details/NPTEL" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SWAYAM's NPTEL page</a> states. The bigger prize is credit. UGC's 2021 credit framework
    lets universities allow up to 40% of the courses in a semester to be taken through SWAYAM, up from 20%
    earlier. In July 2026 UGC urged institutions to map SWAYAM courses for the July semester. But your own
    university must approve the course and decide how credits transfer.
  </p>

  <div class="honest-take">
    <p class="honest-take__label">Honest take</p>
    <p>
      Reports have found that many universities list SWAYAM courses but few students use the credit
      route. That means you may have to ask your department directly. Walk in with one course name and one
      question: "Will this count for credit if I pass the exam?" Get the answer in writing.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="rung-4">Rung 4: institute certificates and the fee trap</h2>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/college-degrees/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students-mistakes-rung-institute-certificates-fee.webp" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Fee-trap panel comparing institute certificate pricing with the stronger test of syllabus, practice, assessment, and work proof" title="Rung 4: institute certificates and the fee trap" />
    <figcaption>A higher fee is justified only when it buys practice, feedback, or proof—not a different logo on paper.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    Local and online institutes sell courses in Tally with GST, Advanced Excel, Power BI, and SAP FICO.
    These can teach you real skills. The certificate itself carries the least weight, and the fee range
    for the same subject is huge.
  </p>

  <div class="feature-grid">
    {feeTrapRows.map((item) => (
