  <h2 id="validity">When to take each one: the validity clock</h2>

  <figure class="article-visual">
    <img src="/images/blog/college-degrees/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students/certificate-courses-for-bcom-students-chronological-take-each-one-validity.webp" width="1600" height="1000" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Timeline showing when to take college-credit, Tally, PL-300, NISM, and SEBI certificates around their validity periods" title="When to take each one: the validity clock" />
    <figcaption>Time expiring certificates near the job search; take durable learning and college-credit routes earlier.</figcaption>
  </figure>

  <p>
    Some certificates carry an expiry date that starts on the day you pass. A NISM exam passed on day one of a three-year BCom
    lapses on graduation day. NISM also says a certificate that has lapsed cannot be renewed. It can be kept alive by passing again
    or completing NISM's continuing professional education before the date.
  </p>

  <div class="comparison-grid">
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--teal">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Safe to take early</div>
      <ul>
        <li>SWAYAM and NPTEL courses that your college approves. Credit is the goal, and they teach you what you like.</li>
        <li>Tally certification. Tally Education says it has lifetime validity.</li>
        <li>PL-300, once you have two dashboards. It renews every 12 months at no cost through an online assessment.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="compare-card compare-card--gold">
      <div class="compare-card__label">Time it close to your job search</div>
      <ul>
        <li>NISM exams. Valid for 3 years from the exam date, so book them in your last two years.</li>
        <li>SEBI Investor Awareness Test. Free, but valid for only 2 years.</li>
        <li>Anything sold as "lifetime" by an institute. Ask who checks it when an employer phones.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

