  <h2 id="questions">Questions BCom students ask most</h2>

  <div class="accordion">
    <details>
      <summary>Is Tally plus Excel enough to get a job after BCom?</summary>
      <div class="accordion-body">
        <p>It is enough to start applying for junior accounts roles, not enough to stand out. Add proof: a year of entries for a small shop, a bank reconciliation, and a one-page summary of what you found. Then the certificate backs up the work.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Which items should I learn with Tally, like GST and Excel?</summary>
      <div class="accordion-body">
        <p>Learn TallyPrime entries first, then GST entries and returns knowledge, then Excel lookups and pivot tables for checking the data. The Tally Bookkeeper course on Coursera already covers accounting basics, payables and receivables, and GST.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Can a BCom graduate become a GST practitioner, and is the exam compulsory?</summary>
      <div class="accordion-body">
        <p>A commerce degree is on the Rule 83 list. Enrolment depends on an NACIN exam, but the last sitting on record was in December 2019. Confirm the current status on the GST portal and the NACIN site before you pay anyone.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What is the scope of a banking certificate after BCom?</summary>
      <div class="accordion-body">
        <p>A private institute&#39;s banking certificate is Rung 4. The regulated route is a NISM exam, and bank jobs themselves are decided by recruitment exams, not by a certificate. Use the certificate to prepare for sales and advisory roles.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>Is NISM study material free?</summary>
      <div class="accordion-body">
        <p>NISM gives free soft-copy workbooks after enrolment for the mutual fund distributor exam. Printed copies are sold separately.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
    <details>
      <summary>What are the best certification courses along with a BCom?</summary>
      <div class="accordion-body">
        <p>It depends on the lane you pick: NISM for markets, Tally for accounts, Power BI for reporting. Use the lane cost table above to check what each costs.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </div>

